bl31.bin -- the BL31 that bootm (bl31_handoff.c) hands the Hi3519DV500 secure
loader before it starts the kernel. Linked into U-Boot by bl31_blob.S.

Built from the vendor SDK's ARM Trusted Firmware, not taken from a flash dump:

  SDK      Hi3519DV500_SDK_V2.0.1.1, package/open_source.tgz
  sources  open_source/arm-trusted-firmware/arm-trusted-firmware-2.7.tar.gz
           + open_source/arm-trusted-firmware/arm-trusted-firmware-2.7.patch
  command  make CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu- PLAT=hi3519dv500 SPD=none \
                CCI_UP=0 BL33_SEC=0 bl31
           (the SDK's own: open_source/arm-trusted-firmware/Makefile, no TEE)
  compiler aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc 16.2.0
  change   --no-warn-rwx-segments added to the `--fatal-warnings -O1` line of
           TF-A's Makefile: binutils 2.39 and later warn that bl31.elf has an
           RWX LOAD segment, which TF-A 2.7 links as fatal (TF-A fixed this
           upstream after 2.7)
  output   build/hi3519dv500/release/bl31.bin, 28945 bytes
  sha256   920fbc52a370fc9a1dfc65083c35bdbd35877c611989149f1d42c68a9942340c

The vendor patch itself carries one prebuilt object,
plat/vendor/hi3519dv500/drivers/nmi/nmi_private.o, which the build links as is.

It is the same size as the BL31 a Taobao Hi3519DV500 kit shipped in its `bl31`
NAND partition (28945 bytes; vendor build, differing only in code generation),
and it loads at the secure loader's BL31_BASE, 0x40010000 (BL31_BASE in
gsl_hi3519dv500/include/platform.h and in TF-A's plat/vendor/hi3519dv500).
